#: src/ui.rs:128
msgid "EPS only, voice-centric: the phone uses only the 4G/5G network and puts calls first: where VoLTE is missing, it is not content with data alone. On a network without 2G/3G this does not help; the usual choice there is the next one."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui.rs:130
msgid "EPS only, data-centric: the phone uses only the 4G/5G network and puts data first. It stays registered on a carrier that has no 2G/3G network for this phone, such as China Telecom. Calls then need VoLTE: without it, no calls are possible."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui.rs:132
msgid "EPS and non-EPS, voice-centric: the phone uses 4G/5G and also the old 2G/3G network for calls and SMS, and puts calls first. This is the modem's own default. It is right where the carrier has a 2G/3G network. Where it has none, as with China Telecom, the registration drops every few minutes: the network refuses with “CS domain not available”."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui.rs:134
msgid "EPS and non-EPS, data-centric: the phone uses 4G/5G and the old 2G/3G network, and puts data first. Right where the carrier has a 2G/3G network and data matters more than calls. Where it has none, the registration drops every few minutes, as with the previous one."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui.rs:143
msgid "EPS: the 4G and 5G network. Everything on it is data."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui.rs:144
msgid "Non-EPS, or the circuit-switched (CS) domain: the older 2G and 3G network, made for calls and SMS."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui.rs:146
msgid "PS only: the phone asks for data service only, so it registers on 4G/5G alone."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui.rs:147
msgid "CS and PS: the phone asks for calls and SMS as well, so it also registers on 2G/3G."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui.rs:148
msgid "Voice-centric: calls come first. The phone wants a network on which it can call."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui.rs:149
msgid "Data-centric: data comes first. The phone stays on 4G/5G even where it could not call."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui.rs:151
msgid "VoLTE: calls over the 4G/5G network, with no 2G/3G network behind them."
msgstr ""

